.TH CD 1
.SH NAME
cd, pwd \- change or show the current directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cd
.RI [ dir ]
.br
.B pwd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cd
and
.B pwd
are commands built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
.B cd
makes
.I dir
the current directory: the one relative paths start from, for the shell
and the programs it starts. Without
.IR dir ,
it goes to the user's home (from
.BR /etc/users ).
.B pwd
prints the current directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if the directory cannot be entered.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR sh (1)
